% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Segmentation of the current run (pass 1).  Positions 1..n of the run are
% \xjp@r@<ctx>@<i> (the character) and \xjp@n@<ctx>@<i> (its index in the
% block); both are freed once the run is done.  These and the marks
% \xjp@s@<n> are global and are set to \relax after use rather than
% undefined: that frees their contents but keeps the names, since creating a
% name inside a group costs a slot of TeX's save stack.  The run is split
% into the fewest words, then the fewest single characters; on a tie the
% longer final word wins.  Costs are 100000 per segment + 1 per single
% character.  The mark for character <n> is stored in \xjp@s@<n>.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
